      "message": "Let\u0027s think about `sbrk()` implementation for a while.\n\nIt uses memory that we know it\u0027s not statically allocated (all addresses after `__shared_mem_buf`) but is not reserved for jump data and panic data (which are stored at the end of SRAM). To determine size of that memory, we use `shared_mem_size()` which later calls `system_usable_ram_end()`.\n\nThe `system_usable_ram_end()` function is EC specific because it depends on jump data which is EC specific construct. Code in `zephyr` directory shouldn\u0027t depend on EC code. It means that either we should provide implementation that doesn\u0027t use EC code (not possible due to jump data) or we can\u0027t move `sbrk.c` here.\n\nI liked this idea, but it will eventually introduce more confusion, so I would just leave it as it is. Sorry for not mentioning about it earlier.\n\nOn the other hand, `exit()` can be implemented using Zephyr calls, so we can put it under `zephyr/libc/exit.c`.",
